# Chat service environment

Annotated reference for the whole set: the repository-root `.env.example`.
This file lists only what `chat-service` reads.

```
APP_ENV=dev
LOG_LEVEL=info

# --- HTTP -------------------------------------------------------------------
HTTP_ADDR=:8080
# Optional CORS allowlist (comma separated). Empty disables cross-origin access.
# HTTP_CORS_ALLOW_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:5173

# --- Retrieval --------------------------------------------------------------
# Ranking weights. These encode a product decision — how far a soft match may
# reorder a hard-filtered list — so they are configuration rather than constants.
# RETRIEVAL_TOP_K=5
# RETRIEVAL_OVERSAMPLE=2
# RETRIEVAL_WEIGHT_STRUCTURED=1.0
# RETRIEVAL_WEIGHT_KEYWORD=0.5
# RETRIEVAL_WEIGHT_VECTOR=1.0
# RETRIEVAL_WEIGHT_QUALITY=0.2
# Per-channel switches, for A/B comparison and for running without one channel.
# RETRIEVAL_ENABLE_STRUCTURED=true
# RETRIEVAL_ENABLE_KEYWORD=true
# The vector channel needs an embedding provider below and an index built by the
# data pipeline. Turning it off is how a deployment runs before either exists.
# RETRIEVAL_ENABLE_VECTOR=true
# Bounds the on-demand query embedding. Separate from REQUEST_TIMEOUT because
# that default is sized for embedding a batch of long documents on a CPU model;
# an online recall embeds one short string.
# RETRIEVAL_EMBEDDING_TIMEOUT=5s

# Optional reranking. Leaving the provider unset switches the stage off, which is
# a supported way to run; MVP does not require a rerank model.
# RERANK_PROVIDER=
# RERANK_MODEL=
# RERANK_TIMEOUT=3s

# --- Chat provider (OpenAI-compatible) ---------------------------------------
# CHAT_PROVIDER=openai_compatible
# CHAT_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# CHAT_API_KEY=<secret>
# CHAT_MODEL=<tool-capable-model-id>
# Optional per-request headers as JSON (e.g. OpenRouter attribution headers).
# CHAT_EXTRA_HEADERS_JSON={"X-Title":"PlatePilot","HTTP-Referer":"http://localhost:8080"}
# Bounds one non-streaming attempt; streaming calls follow the request context.
# CHAT_TIMEOUT=60s
# Additional attempts after the first one for 429/408/5xx/transport errors.
# 0 disables retries.
# CHAT_MAX_RETRIES=2
# Capability table — must match what the chosen model actually supports.
# CHAT_SUPPORTS_TOOLS=true
# CHAT_SUPPORTS_PARALLEL_TOOLS=false
# CHAT_SUPPORTS_JSON_SCHEMA=false
# CHAT_CONTEXT_TOKENS=32768

# --- Agent runtime -----------------------------------------------------------
# Maximum plan->tools cycles per turn before the model is forced to answer.
# AGENT_MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS=5
# Bound on one tool invocation (search/evidence retrieval).
# AGENT_TOOL_TIMEOUT=15s

# --- Admin console (/admin/v1/*) ---------------------------------------------
# Disabled by default. When enabled the routes are additionally restricted to
# loopback peers (the serving process's local host); forwarded headers are not
# trusted. With it disabled the paths return 404.
# ADMIN_ENABLED=false
# ADMIN_DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE=25
# ADMIN_MAX_PAGE_SIZE=100
# Maximum rejection rows returned on one batch detail.
# ADMIN_MAX_REJECTIONS=200

# --- Shared with data-pipeline ------------------------------------------------
# PostgreSQL. Start it with: docker compose -f ../deploy/docker-compose.yml up -d
# Migrations are applied by `make -C ../data-pipeline migrate`.
POSTGRES_DSN=postgres://platepilot:platepilot@localhost:55432/platepilot?sslmode=disable
POSTGRES_DATABASE=platepilot
# Optional connection-pool / connect-timeout tuning
# POSTGRES_TIMEOUT=30s
# POSTGRES_CONNECT_TIMEOUT=10s
# POSTGRES_MAX_POOL_SIZE=8
# POSTGRES_MIN_POOL_SIZE=0

# Local Ollama embedding (required for the vector channel)
# EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=ollama
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
# EMBEDDING_MODEL=qwen3-embedding:0.6b
# EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS=1024
```
